  "planning_notes": [
    "Board is arduino:avr:uno with wiring: LM35 -> A1 (analog input), Fan PWM -> D5 (PWM output), Overheat LED -> D13 (digital output active-high).",
    "Serial uses baud 9600 with framing=line_or_idle and idle_timeout_ms=20 per requirement.",
    "LM35 calibration and conversion to °C are handled in the SysML model; the analog_input port carries raw ADC counts (no fabricated electrical calibration requested here).",
    "Fan control logic (target threshold and minimum fan speed configured via serial) and overheat LED behavior are handled in the SysML model; this interface proposal only provides the required IO ports.",
    "Control period chosen as 10 ms as scheduling granularity; temperature sampling uses a multiple of control step (40 ms).",
    "Overheat warning serial trigger is modeled as a Boolean gate; the reported value is the current calibrated temperature in °C.",
    "Serial command mapping: io_3.commands maps 1..32 exact printable ASCII tokens to i32 codes; tokens are assumed to be uppercase ASCII with underscores and are handled by the SysML model."
